Fix the column name that stops FoamBench's own scoring script.

`execution_report.py` writes its result under the column `Success`:

    pd.DataFrame(basic_results, columns=["Dataset", "Directory", "Success"])

and `score_calculation.py` reads it as `Execution`, so the final scoring raises
KeyError: 'Execution' before writing anything. Both files are from
NLR-Theseus/cfdllmbench (main, fetched 2026-08-04).

Applies to FoamBench/score_calculation.py:

    cd ~/foambench && patch -p0 < scripts/bench/score_calculation.patch

--- score_calculation.py
+++ score_calculation.py
@@ -25,10 +25,10 @@
     nmse_df["NMSE_Score"] = nmse_df["NMSE"].apply(score_nmse)

     merged = exec_df.merge(sim_df, on="key").merge(nmse_df, on="key")
-    merged["Success_Score"] = ((merged["Execution"] == 1) & (merged["NMSE_Score"] == 1)).astype(float)
+    merged["Success_Score"] = ((merged["Success"] == 1) & (merged["NMSE_Score"] == 1)).astype(float)

     return pd.DataFrame({
         "Split": [split_name],
-        "Execution Score": [merged["Execution"].mean()],
+        "Execution Score": [merged["Success"].mean()],
         "CodeBLEU Score": [merged["CodeBLEU"].mean()],
         "Tree Score": [merged["TreeScore"].mean()],
         "NMSE Score": [merged["NMSE_Score"].mean()],
